alse,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0065. The Executor log is filled in and the packet resolves the issues raised in both earlier rejections.\n\n- **The goal is met as far as it can be.** `external/core` is still read-only, so the packet's fallback applies: a decision note for humans plus, where needed, a patch. The note is `.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-0065-x2t-js-snapshots.md`. The executor showed that no `core` change is needed, because the installed x2t (9.3.7-1) already loads `sdk-all.bin` snapshots. Dropping the earlier patch, whose malformed hunk header was the first rejection, is therefore justified.\n- **Speed is proven, which was the second rejection.** I spot-checked the raw `convert-large` JSON and it matches the note: 631 / 621 / 909 ms for new.docx / new.xlsx / new.pptx with the snapshots, about 88–106 ms faster to PDF than without. Conversions that don't run the JavaScript engine serve as a control and show no gain.\n- **The shortfall is reported honestly.** The gain is about 0.1 s, below the plan's 0.3–0.6 s estimate. The log says so and explains why: the rest of the fixed cost is the JavaScript warming up during the first conversion step.\n- **Output is unchanged.** The corpus oracle gives `equal` against `baseline-9.3.7-1.json`.\n- **The contract holds.** Only files under `.theseus/` changed, so nothing in `contract.preserve` was touched. The diff is 6 files and 130 lines, at the 6-file limit and well under 800 lines.\n- **The follow-up is requested.** `.theseus/spawn/PKT-0065-ship-v8-js-startup-snapshots-*.md` asks for the install and upgrade step to generate the snapshots as user `ds`. It covers the two risks the note identifies: snapshots go stale after an upgrade, and they must be owned by `ds`. The Spawned packets section is empty, but the spawn file is enough under TEP-0004.\n- **Surprises, lessons and friction are recorded.** The flaky `docsCoServerCrashPaths` test is noted as outside the target. That characterize-packet rule doesn't apply here, because this is a refactor packet.\n\nThere's one small gap, which doesn't block approval. The packet claims the gain is about the same 0.1 s on large files, but that was never measured. The new packet should measure it.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE The decision note and spawned packaging follow-up are measured and faithful to the goal: snapshots speed up small PDF exports by about 0.1 s with equal corpus output, and both earlier rejections are resolved.","ttft_ms":2769,"type":"result","duration_ms":19307,"uuid":"898cc687-65ba-480a-9f40-51aa30b2874e","ttft_stream_ms":1023,"time_to_request_ms":393,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":234,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":18,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":39,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":9,"auto_mode_context_wait":8,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":25,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":5,"request_build":11},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":68,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":185,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":214,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":227,"process_anon_mib_result":139,"process_peak_rss_mib":261,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1061,"process_wall_ms_turn":19306,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":439,"process_wall_ms_streaming":15773,"main_stream_count":5,"main_stream_event_count":305,"main_stream_chunk_count":110,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":7,"cpu_ms":20,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":7,"ambient_wait_ms":6,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":1023,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":21207287,"warm_spare_c